FOCUS ONLY ON THE CRYSTAL SYSTEM AFTER BOSS COMPLETION.

IMPORTANT: The current progression flow is working correctly. DO NOT break or redesign it.

The current flow is:

Lesson 1 → Minion 1 → Lesson 2 → Minion 2 → Lesson 3 → Minion 3 → Boss 1 → Home → Lesson 4

KEEP THIS FLOW EXACTLY AS IT IS.

Now I want to make the crystals an important part of the progression and lore.

After defeating a boss, the player receives the boss's crystals. These crystals should NOT simply be treated as a reward that disappears into the inventory.

The player should have to USE/PLACE the collected crystals somewhere meaningful in the world.

LORE/PROGRESSION IDEA:

The tower's floors are dark/inactive because of the Oblivion Storm.

When the player defeats a boss and obtains its crystals, those crystals can be placed into the tower's corresponding mechanism/core/seal/altar — whatever existing lore terminology and visual design best fits the game.

Placing the required crystals should:

1. Consume/use the collected crystals appropriately.
2. Activate/illuminate the corresponding tower floor.
3. Visually communicate that the floor has been CLEARED and restored.
4. Unlock/enable progression toward the next floor/boss.
5. Make the crystals feel like an actual gameplay/progression mechanic rather than just an ordinary reward.

For example:

Boss 1 defeated
→ player receives the required crystals
→ player places the crystals into the appropriate tower mechanism
→ Floor 1 becomes illuminated/restored
→ the path toward Floor 2 becomes available
→ the player can continue their journey.

The same concept should be scalable for later floors:

Boss 2 → crystals → activate Floor 2
Boss 3 → crystals → activate Floor 3
Boss 4 → crystals → activate Floor 4
etc.

IMPORTANT:
Do NOT redesign the existing progression flow.

Do NOT make the crystal interaction block the currently working lesson/minion/boss sequence in an awkward way.

Instead, integrate the crystal placement naturally into the existing post-boss sequence.

The player should clearly understand:
"I defeated this boss, obtained its crystals, and now I need to restore/illuminate this part of the tower."

Please inspect the existing Tower UI, boss progression, crystal/reward logic, and lore-related elements before implementing this.

If there is already an appropriate place/mechanism in the existing design for placing the crystals, use it instead of inventing an unrelated interface.

The visual result should make it obvious that the floor has changed from DARK/INACTIVE → RESTORED/ILLUMINATED after the crystals are placed.

Most importantly, the crystal placement should have REAL progression/state behind it, not just be a visual animation.

Test that:

Boss 1 completed
→ crystals obtained
→ crystals can be placed
→ Floor 1 becomes illuminated/restored
→ progression toward the next floor remains available
→ returning to Home still correctly continues the player's journey.

DO NOT modify unrelated features in this task.
